\f1\fs22 Worse, it had arrived by email, which gave Hardy to swearing, which he rarely did. It would mean several more data centres\'92 worth of solution architecture would need to be scrapped before this whole sorry thing had run its course\'97just to eradicate one report let loose on the company mail servers\'97but that expense was nothing compared to the alternative collapse of industries Hardy expected the report to predict. What made him swear: he was sure the tablet he\'92d give the juniors was battened down tighter than that.\
The report was competent. It had an executive summary of a page and a half. It had an assumptions page, properly caveated. It had three scenarios, named Base, Super Base and Woofer Bass, with sensitivities set out in a table that had clearly been fought over. It had a risk register. It had an appendix, running to sixty pages, of the kind that consulting firms included to make sure the client gave up and accepted whatever the firm asked for.\
It was dispassionate. Hardy could see that not a word of it was drafted in anger. The juniors arrived at it. They checked it. They were quietly pleased with its cleanliness and its adherence to company style guides and layout themes.\
Its recommendation was simple: Woofer Base was the only viable option. Dr Hermann\'92s miracle drug (dubbed 
\f2\i Mama Koka
\f1\i0  in the report\'97one of the juniors was clearly showing off) must be destroyed, all research must be destroyed, and all related research staff must be\'85\
Hardy scrolled to the next page.\
